# AQP Index (sole-writer tree)

`aqp_index/` is AQP's single source of truth for project orientation:
the centralized index, SSoT architecture pointers, the consolidated
configuration set, token-saving code indices, the project skills
registry, and the subagent registry.

## Sole writer

The only agent permitted to write inside this tree is the
[aqp-index-curator](mdc:.cursor/agents/aqp-index-curator.md) subagent.

All other agents — Cursor, subagents, and humans operating through
Cursor — have **read-only** access to this folder. The single
documented exception is appending or fixing a one-liner pointer in
repo-root [README.md](mdc:README.md) or [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) that
orients readers into `aqp_index/`.

## Curator invariants

The curator MUST:

1. Cite a specific file path for every claim. No fabrication. If a
   claim cannot be verified, write a `// TODO: verify <reason>` block
   and open a note in `.cursor/plans/`.
2. Stamp every refreshed file with a top-of-file `> Last refreshed:
   YYYY-MM-DD by aqp-index-curator` line.
3. Generate code indices as signatures only (class / function names + a
   one-line docstring slice, with `path:line` citations). Never paste
   function bodies.
4. Respect AQP rules 1-47 (see [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md)). Never edit
   Python source, migrations, or production configs from this role.
5. Refresh on a qualifying trigger: any commit touching
   [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md), [.cursor/rules/](mdc:.cursor/rules),
   [aqp_docs/](mdc:aqp_docs), [configs/](mdc:configs), or the public
   surface of any `aqp_*` package.

## Read-only contract for everyone else

Other agents reading from here SHOULD:

- Prefer `aqp_index/code-index/*.md` to scanning source files when
  only signatures are needed; this is the explicit token-saving win.
- Link to `aqp_index/architecture/*.md` for canonical orientation.
- Open a `.cursor/plans/` note (rather than editing here directly)
  when they notice stale content.

## Procedure

The curator's pass procedure is documented at
[aqp_index/skills/aqp-index-curator-skill.md](mdc:aqp_index/skills/aqp-index-curator-skill.md):
Plan -> Scan -> Diff -> Refresh -> Validate.
